    "chunk_text": "Gomez himself set out the underlying philosophy in 2021, arguing that Sri Lanka\u2019s coastal tourism should embrace a less-is-more approach. He called for plots of roughly an acre carrying a handful of carefully designed units over less than half the land, and buildings no taller than five storeys so as to stay beneath the line of the coastal coconut palms. He also wanted hospitality that leans on local cooking and local character. Conceived some 15 years earlier, Aditya reads as an early built argument for the same view.\n\n\u201cWe are so proud to be the front runners of the boutique hospitality space, which Sri Lanka has come to be known for,\u201d Dawoodbhoy noted in a statement issued to mark the anniversary.\n\n\u201cTheir skills are in demand in industries today. The fact that they choose to be with us ensures the quality and consistency of our product,\u201d he added.\n\nDirector and General Manager Shamindra Fernando, who was already co-managing the hotel in its first year, embodies that continuity. The event\u2019s master of ceremonies observed that repeat guests often arrive asking for staff members by name, describing it as a culture built on passion that has carried the property through two decades.\n\nThat loyalty was tested during the economic crisis. Akbarally told guests the team had braced for a 20 percent salary cut, a cost he said the Managing Director absorbed himself, with salaries paid in full throughout the downturn.\n\n\u201cWe know their families, we know their children, and they are part of our family,\u201d he remarked.\n\nHe added that the management continues to meet staff to improve and add facilities for them.\n\nFernando noted that the team is drawn almost entirely from the resort\u2019s immediate surroundings, describing the jobs as a source of income and professional standing for the community around Rathgama."
