    "date_str": "2026-10-31",
    "description": "Why are investors fleeing? China SOE Exit From Colombo Logistical Hub",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Why-are-investors-fleeing-China-SOE-Exit-From-Colombo-Logistical-Hub/172-353851",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1793430275.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-10-31-dailymirrorlk-82b94cde-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "571753843bcb6bebd8b0d7e355ef4a43",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1716,
    "chunk_text": "Why are investors fleeing? China SOE Exit From Colombo Logistical Hub\n\nRegular abandonment of high-profile projects does not augur well for investment confidence in Sri Lanka\n\nThe recent exit of China Merchant Holdings from a\u00a0 $392 million logistics hub in the Colombo Port City has yet again highlighted the usual script of high-profile investments announced with much fanfare collapsing under the weight of intractable regulatory bottlenecks.\n\nThe South Asia Commercial and Logistics Hub (SACHL), a joint venture between China Port Merchants, which held a 70% stake and Sri Lanka Port Authority, was announced in April 2023 and touted as a gesture of confidence in Colombo Port City while the country was under severe economic crisis.\u00a0 In December the same year, the government officially gazetted it as a Strategic Development Project (SDP), effectively granting lucrative tax concessions including a 15-year total exemption from Corporate income tax, a 15-year exception on withholding taxes and dividend taxes for its shareholders and an exemption from secondary import levies during the construction period.\n\nHowever, the project ran into troubled waters in 2024 when the IMF bailout conditions required the government to curb various tax concessions. The project, slated to be completed by the end of last year, has been stalled since then, while the government sought to bypass the IMF conditionalities by rerouting the project through the BOI.\n\nHowever, in the end, the regular bureaucratic and regulatory bottlenecks and protracted inter-departmental wrangling ( On this occasion, between the Ministry of Finance, Port authorities and Inland Revenue Department) seemed to have hit the nail in the coffin."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-10-31-dailymirrorlk-82b94cde",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-82b94cde",
    "date_str": "2026-10-31",
    "description": "Why are investors fleeing? China SOE Exit From Colombo Logistical Hub",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/opinion/Why-are-investors-fleeing-China-SOE-Exit-From-Colombo-Logistical-Hub/172-353851",
    "lang": "en",
