    "chunk_text": "Japan has insisted on legally binding guarantees for transparency, predictability and non-discrimination. The recent Investment Protection Act and the proposed Public Private Partnership Bill are intended to address some of the deep-rooted bureaucratic bottlenecks.\n\nThe NPP/ JVP government, when in opposition, blamed corruption for the flight of foreign investment and low economic growth. However, in power, it must be aware that economic growth is faltering under its watch, hitting 4.2 per cent in the second quarter. Its commitment to a complete overhaul of institutional and regulatory mechanisms for investment is praiseworthy. However, proof of pudding is in the eating, and as of now, it has delivered very little, other than managing the economic recovery, which, to give the devil its due, is Ranil Wickremesinghe\u2019s achievement. That momentum is now faltering, and unless the government pushes forward with long-delayed economic reforms, Sri Lanka would likely head towards yet another period of suppressed economic growth, similar to the five years of Yahapalanaya."
